<!--
    RfKeybindActionDialog - FS25_SettingsHub
    The Realistic Farming Control Center.

    Pattern: emptyPanel row containers with fixed slots plus pagination, the
    idiom proven by SoilReportDialog and DepotDialog. Text cells at an
    intermediate X MUST sit inside a row container or they will not position.
    Rows are a fixed pool filled from Lua, not created at runtime, so a session
    with 3 mods and one with 20 use the same layout and only the page count
    changes.

    COLUMN GEOMETRY. The row container is 880px wide, half-width 440. Each
    column is defined by an explicit LEFT EDGE and its centre is derived from
    its own width. This matters: elements anchor at their centre, so a header
    250px wide and a data cell 170px wide sharing one position start their
    left-aligned text 40px apart, which is exactly how the headings drifted out
    of line. Header and data profiles now share a width per column.

      Column   Width   Left edge   Centre
      Module   170px   -430px       -345px
      Action   260px   -250px       -120px
      Key      160px    +30px        110px
      Trigger  120px   +250px        310px

    Rightmost edge is +370px, inside the 440px half-width, so nothing overhangs.

    Y LAYOUT. Elements anchor top-down and occupy their full height, so a
    separator has to clear the BOTTOM of the element above it, not just its
    position. The title sits at -18 and is 24px tall, so it occupies -18 to -42;
    the first separator is at -50, clear of it. The old layout put that
    separator at -34, inside the title box, which drew a line through the title,
    and put another one inside the pagination row.

      -18  : title           -50  : separator
      -60  : header row      -84  : separator
      -92  : rows 0..24 at 20px, last row ends -592
      -600 : separator       -608 : pagination
      -638 : separator       -646 : summon hint
      -666 : status

    Trigger buttons extend fs25_wideButton, NOT buttonActivate. buttonActivate
    inherits inputAction MENU_ACTIVATE and therefore paints a SPACE key chip
    that shoves its own label out of its box onto the neighbouring cell.
    fs25_wideButton is buttonActivate's own base minus the inputAction: same
    chrome, no chip, and mouse onClick is unaffected because it never used the
    action. Proven live 2026-08-22.
-->
